  "meta": {
    "name": "qwen3-next-80b-a3b",
    "family": "qwen",
    "notes": "Three layers in four are gated DeltaNet and the fourth is ordinary attention, so only twelve of the forty-eight hold a cache that grows with the sequence; the other thirty-six carry a fixed state per sequence. The linear layers have twice as many value heads as key heads, which is most of why their input projection is 12,288 wide. The attention layers gate their own output with a projection as wide as the queries, which is why `q_proj` is [8192, 2048] rather than [4096, 2048]. Every layer is a mixture of 512 experts with ten routed and one shared, so 3.0B of the 79.7B is active per token. The checkpoint also ships a multi-token-prediction head of 1.65B, which is not modelled here because it is not part of the model you serve.",
    "published": {
      "params": 79674391296,
      "source": "https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct"
    }
  },
